    ("h2", "Who can come with you"),
    ("p", "Most Indian master's students cannot bring dependants, and this is the rule people discover too late. A partner or child can come only if you are on a government-sponsored course lasting more than six months, or a postgraduate research course at a higher education provider with a track record of compliance. Part-time students cannot bring dependants at all. If your plan involves a spouse joining you on a one-year taught master's, that plan does not exist under these rules."),
