    ("h2", "How to answer"),
    ("p", "Be specific and short. 'The course has a module on applied econometrics that uses the same Bank of England datasets I used in my dissertation' is an answer. 'It is a world-class university with global exposure' is a sentence from a brochure and it invites the next question. Officers are told not to refuse people for not knowing local geography or bus routes - the test is whether your decision makes sense, not whether you have memorised trivia."),
    ("p", "Two hard rules. If you miss the interview without a reason the Home Office accepts, the application must be refused. And if the Home Office finds you used deception - false documents, a false statement, a bank balance that was not yours - refusal is mandatory and future applications face a long ban, commonly ten years. No consultancy can fix that, and the ones that promise to are the reason it happens."),
